I put my phone on the table and relax.
Suddenly there is a quick knock on my door.
It interrupts my thoughts.
I get up from the sofa and walk out into the hallway.
When I open the door, Nina is standing out in the hall.
She has a small cardboard box in her hands.
"Hi Maya, I have a package for you," she says and smiles.
She hands me the box.
"It was delivered to my place earlier this afternoon," Nina explains.
"The mail carrier must have accidentally mixed up our doors."
I look at the box and see my name on it.
"Oh!"
"It is my new coffee beans!"
"I usually buy them online," I tell her.
"Normally packages are left down in the lobby," Nina says.
"Yes, they usually get put there," I reply.
I accept the cardboard box with a big smile.
It already smells faintly of roasted coffee.
"Thank you so much for bringing it over," I say.
